# CRLF in a file git judges to be text is stored and checked out as LF on every system; a file
# with a lone carriage return counts as binary and keeps its bytes (git 2.53, seen 2026-10-08).
# This reaches the corpus: an expectation is compared byte for byte, so a case that expects a
# carriage-return byte marks its path `-text` here.
* text=auto eol=lf
